{
  "scenario": "The residential tenancy of the LKIF Core sample, written in all three standards. The statute's obligation on landlords to keep the dwelling in repair, the tenant's permission to withhold rent once they have given notice of disrepair, and the prohibition on evicting without a court order are added as LegalRuleML deontic specifications, borne by the landlord and tenant and associated with the statute as their legal source and the legislature as their authority, and as an ODRL Set policy over the dwelling, where the notice becomes a duty to inform the landlord that the permission carries. The lease becomes an ODRL Agreement granting the tenant the use of the dwelling and the duty to pay rent. Sections 30 and 95 of the LegalRuleML sample's Residential Tenancies (Example) Act 2024 are added to ODRL in turn: the tenant's obligation to pay rent, with the late fee as its consequence, and the landlord's prohibition on entering the premises. Nodes that are the same individual carry the same IRI in every standard and are linked by SAME_AS; the late fee duty and the lease agreement are only RELATED_TO the LegalRuleML penalty statement and the LKIF contract. The ODRL sample's music licence describes nothing else here, so it is not linked.",
